MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience equivalent to the next lower grade level (GS-12) or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector performing work that involves recruiting, examining, selecting and placing employees; performing job analysis; workforce planning and analysis; and advising management in identifying, attracting, and retaining a high-quality and diverse workforce that is capable of accomplishing the organization's mission; and work that involves position evaluation, establishing and maintaining a position classification program to determine appropriate pay system, occupational grouping, title and grade of positions, and advising on position and organization design. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following:
1) Leading team members by assessing skill levels and occupational specialization to assist with the distribution and balance of workload;
2) Advising management on recruitment/placement strategies, position classification, organizational structure and strategic planning;
3) Providing advice and assistance on the proper assessment of candidates with a focus on appropriate assessment tools;
4) Interpreting and applying classification standards/guides to reach sound classification decisions;
5) Providing guidance on approaches to pay and compensation to ensure compliance with policies and procedures;
6) Providing strategic HR advice and guidance to senior management in order to execute HR plans. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

In order to qualify for this position, your resume must provide sufficient experience and/or knowledge, skills, and abilities to perform the duties of the specific position for which you are being considered. Your resume is the key means we have for evaluating your skills, knowledge, and abilities as they relate to this position. Therefore, we encourage you to be clear and specific when describing your experience. Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the (NT-2 or GS-11) grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: To be considered for NT-03: 1) Coordinating, controlling, executing, and managing multiple priority tasks to include assignment and tracking to completion;
2) Developing, disseminating, and maintaining compensation and classification policies, procedures, strategy, and work products;
3) Applying federal position management and classification policies;
4) Interpreting and applying position classification standards to determine the series, titles, and grades of various positions within an organization;
5) Advising and guiding management on position management and classification regulations, policies and standards; and
6) Preparing written documents used in support of an organization's position management or classification mission requirements. NOTE: This experience must be fully and clearly supported in your resume. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-5 grade level or NT-2 pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Independently researches and prepares documentation in support of Agency responses to Unfair Labor Practice (ULP) charges, petitions for unit recognition, amendments and/or decertification proceedings;
2) Serving as chief negotiator to implement collective bargaining agreement(s) and providing guidance on Bargaining Unit Status (BUS) Code Determinations;
3) Managing command performance management systems for General Schedule, Federal Wage Standard, and Demonstration Project personnel; and
4) Independently preparing documents for third party review (counsel, FLRA, MSPB, EEO). NOTE: This information must be supported in your resume to be considered for the position. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
